218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (Unit testing is the practice of verifying the smallest testable parts of an application, such as functions and methods, in isolation. When it is combined with DevOps, these tests run automatically every time a developer commits code, so defects are detected within minutes rather than late in the release cycle. This project demonstrates Unit Testing using DevOps: a small Python application \(a calculator module\) is covered by automated unit tests written with the unittest framework, stored in a Git repository, and validated by a Continuous Integration \(CI\) pipeline built with GitHub Actions. The pipeline checks out the code, installs dependencies, runs all unit tests, and builds a Docker image only if every test passes. In the experiment, all 8 test cases passed. The project shows how automated testing inside a DevOps pipeline improves code quality, shortens feedback time, and makes software delivery faster and more reliable. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 104 0 R
/Pg 16 0 R
/A [527 0 R 0]
/K [0]
>>
